  "worked_solution": "First, we find the value of the function at $P$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1,0) & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+2(1)+3(0))=\\operatorname{ln}\u20613\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=\\operatorname{ln}\u20613.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}\u2061(x+2y+3z) & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20613 \\\\ x+2y+3z & =3 \\\\ x+2y+3z-3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(1,1,0)$ is the plane $x+2y+3z-3=0.$",
